    #!/usr/bin/env bash
    # Milestone 3 part 2 P1 negative.log (specs/0024-rich-text.md, "P1": "The
    # negative log through the binary: the sample on a fixture from the template
    # whose first sheet's last row is 1048576 (refused with the index message, a
    # control)"). One family, the gate's host debug binary copied into a detached
    # worktree of the phase commit and checked against gate.log's hash, on
    # fictional packages this log builds from the phase commit's template files.
    # The template's worksheet holds an empty sheetData alone and its workbook no
    # shared strings part:
    #
    # (R) --richtext-sample, the template's worksheet's sheetData, and a shared
    #     strings part with its relationship and Override where the case holds
    #     one, set per case:
    #       R0 the bare template: M is 0, the rich value goes on A1, exit 0, its
    #          line;
    #       R1 one row numbered 1048576, the grid's last, holding one number
    #          cell: the sample's cell is past the grid, the index message;
    #       R1C the same with the row numbered 1048575, the control for R1: the
    #          rich value goes on the grid's last row, exit 0, its line;
    #       R2 a shared strings part whose one item has a run whose rPr holds a
    #          b with a val this layer cannot read: the run properties message,
    #          from the table's read;
    #       R2C the same with a plain b, the control for R2: exit 0, its line,
    #          the table's one rich item counted before and after;
    #       R3 an inline string cell on A1 whose run's rPr holds the same b: the
    #          run properties message, from the cell read;
    #       R3C the same with a plain b, the control for R3: exit 0, its line,
    #          the inline rich cell counted before and two after.
    # Each refusal: exit 2, the error line exactly the message the committed
    # source holds, no stdout, no output file. Then the messages of this phase,
    # read from the source by constant name, compared as SETS with those reached
    # here and those the log states unreachable, with the reason and the covering
    # test for each; and usage shapes.
    #
    # CARRIED TO M3 part 2 P1 from M2 part 4d P1's negative script (printed in
    # records/logs/m2p4d-p1/negative.log, byte-identical to its copy kept on the
    # disk under <home>/.cache/emend-build/m2p4d-p1/scripts, which this phase
    # keeps as <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p2-p1/gen/negative-template-m2p4d-p1.sh;
    # its change lists CA to DD stand in that log), edited by hand and grepped for
    # part 4d's tokens in every form (m2p4d, the 4d P1 subjects, a207e175,
    # specs/0022, comment-sample, the C cases, COMMENT_ and COMMENTS_). What
    # differs, and why:
    #  EA. The phase, the log directory, the subjects and the build directories
    #      are M3 part 2 P1's. The base is M3 part 1's close-out record commit
    #      ("M3 part 1 close-out record:"); the doc commit and the three code
    #      commits by their full P1 subjects. The spec pin is specs/0024's blob
    #      at P1's doc commit, ae37a294. The working file holds planning's
    #      uncommitted "Planning rulings during P1"; the status pattern allows
    #      that one line, this phase's logs and its records/m3p2-p1- and
    #      records/m3p2-open- stems.
    #  EB. The family is R0 to R3C above, the generator gen-r.py setting the
    #      template's sheetData per case and adding a shared strings part, its
    #      relationship and its Override where the case holds one. The spec's
    #      refusal with its control is R1 and R1C; R2 and R3 reach this phase's
    #      read message through the binary from the table and from a cell, each
    #      with its control.
    #  EC. The messages of this phase are the two constants from
    #      RICH_TEXT_INVALID to RUN_PROPERTIES_UNREADABLE in the phase commit's
    #      crates/emend/src/cells.rs, where they are raised, read by constant
    #      name; the index message R1 reaches is part 3's, INDEX_OUT_OF_RANGE in
    #      crates/emend/src/package.rs, read by constant name the same way and
    #      not one of this phase's. The reader takes a constant with or without
    #      pub(crate). "a rich text is not valid" is stated unreachable, with
    #      its covering test in package/tests/richtext.rs.
